 },
 "summary": "A single-channel photocoupler in a four-pin DIP: a GaAs infrared LED shining on a silicon NPN phototransistor, with only collector and emitter brought out. The collector-emitter voltage is 80 V minimum and the two sides are tested to 5000 Vrms for 60 s. CTR at IF = 5 mA, VCE = 5 V is 50 % to 600 % unranked and is also sold in eight narrower ranks; rank GB, the TLP785(GB,F, is 100 % to 600 %. TLP785 has 7.62 mm lead rows and 7 mm creepage; TLP785F bends the leads out to 10.16 mm for 8 mm creepage, and both come with surface-mount lead forms.",
