 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A gallium arsenide infrared LED is coupled by light to a silicon phototransistor inside a plastic DIP with four leads. Pins 1 and 2 are the LED, pins 3 and 4 the transistor's emitter and collector; there is no base pin."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Intended for solid-state relays, switch-mode power supplies, office machines, home appliances, general controllers, and carrying signals between circuits at different potentials."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Lead forms",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "TLP785 has its lead rows 7.62 mm apart. TLP785F has the same body with its leads bent out to rows 10.16 mm apart, giving longer creepage for surface mounting. LF6 (on TLP785) and LF7 (on TLP785F) are the surface-mount lead forms."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "LED forward current falls by 0.7 mA/°C and LED dissipation by 0.9 mW/°C above 39 °C; collector dissipation falls by 1.5 mW/°C and total dissipation by 2.4 mW/°C above 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Agency approvals",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "UL1577 and c-UL (CSA Component Acceptance Service No. 5A), file E67349; VDE to DIN EN60747-5-5 when ordered with option (D4); CQC to GB4943.1 and GB8898 (China factory); SEMKO to EN60065, EN60950-1 and EN62368-1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Option (D4)",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Parts tested to EN60747-5-5 carry D4 in the order code, ahead of the CTR rank and lead bend, as in TLP785(D4-GR-LF6,F. For safety-standard listings the plain type name (TLP785) is used. A D4 part carries a 4 on its top face."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "The top face carries the Toshiba mark and lot number, the device name beside a P, the CTR rank marking, the D4 mark where it applies, and a dot at pin 1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ordering code",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "An order names the device, CTR rank, tape type and quantity, for example TLP785(BL-TP6,F at 4000 pieces; tape orders come in multiples of 4000. The trailing F denotes the [[G]]/RoHS-compatible version, and the code may end in an extra letter or digit."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Tape and reel",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "TP6 and TP7 tape hold 2000 parts per reel, two reels to a carton. A reel starts with 30 or more empty pockets and ends with 50 or more. The carton label shows the product number, standard classification symbol, quantity, lot number and the Toshiba name."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reflow soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "The profile is set by package surface temperature: preheat 150 to 200 °C for 60 to 120 s, at most 260 °C peak, no more than 30 s within 5 °C of the peak, 60 to 150 s above 217 °C. Reflow at most twice, and finish all mounting within two weeks of the first pass."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Flow and iron soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Flow: preheat to 150 °C package surface for 60 to 120 s, then 260 °C for no more than 10 s, one pass only. Iron: at most 10 s with the lead at up to 260 °C, or 3 s at up to 350 °C, once per lead."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Keep the parts at 5 °C to 35 °C and 45 % to 75 % relative humidity, away from moisture, direct sun, corrosive gas and dust, and where temperature is steady so no condensation forms on the leads. Use anti-static containers once out of the packing and put no load on the parts. After more than two years in storage, check the leads still solder well."
  }
 ],
